WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.850
Learn to develop an understanding of roman numeral system up xxx (i.e. 30) and count

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:11.123
and convert hindu arabic numerals to roman numerals up to 30 and vice versa

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:18.536
Which Roman numeral represents 1? The answer is I. I equals 1, V equals 5 and X

00:00:18.536 --> 00:00:21.635
equals 10; IV equals 4, IX equals 9.

00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:27.259
A scoreboard uses Roman numbers. Which symbol should appear for position 6? Pause and

00:00:27.259 --> 00:00:29.319
solve it in your exercise book.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:34.232
The answer is VI. Build Roman numerals using X, V and I.
